      ":question/worked-solution": "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- First, we note that $\\sqrt{-25}=5\\text{i}$ is a complex number. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{-25}\\in C\n$$\n\n- Since the imaginary part of $\\sqrt{-25}$ is nonzero, it does *not* belong to $N,Z,Q,$ or $R.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\sqrt{-25}\\notin N\\qquad \\sqrt{-25}\\notin Z \\\\ \\sqrt{-25}\\notin Q\\qquad \\sqrt{-25}\\notin R\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $C$ only."
    },
